---
import PageHero from '@src/components/pages/PageHero.astro';
import PageSection from '@src/components/pages/PageSection.astro';
import Pending from '@src/components/pages/Pending.astro';
import { routes } from '@src/data/routes';
import { site } from '@src/data/site';
import Base from '@src/layouts/Base.astro';
import { lastModified } from '@src/lib/dates';
import { routeSeo } from '@src/lib/seo/meta';

const updated = lastModified(...routes['/about'].sources);
---

<Base seo={routeSeo('/about')}>
  <PageHero
    kicker="about"
    title="Noticing when a person is doing a machine’s job."
    updated={updated}
  >
    <p>
      The short version: community college, then the University of Illinois, then client work in
      Austin. The longer version is that most of what I have built started as somebody, often me,
      doing the same thing by hand for the third time.
    </p>
  </PageHero>

  <PageSection id="route" title="The route here">
    <p>
      I started at Wilbur Wright College and transferred to the University of Illinois
      Urbana-Champaign for a computer science degree, finishing in 2025. Along the way I worked on
      research into mentor–mentee matching, presented it twice, and it was later written up for the
      American Society for Engineering Education.
    </p>
    {/* @TODO: replace with your own account of the community college years and the transfer */}
  </PageSection>

  <PageSection id="operating" title="Running something of my own" ground="body">
    <p>
      Before the engineering jobs there was a reselling operation, and then a small 3D printing
      business: intake, production, fulfilment, and the software to keep all three straight. It is
      where AMS-X comes from. Four spools is a hardware answer to a software problem, and standing
      at a printer to swap filament is exactly the kind of manual step worth deleting.
    </p>
    {/* @TODO: how the printing business actually runs day to day, and what it taught you */}
  </PageSection>

  <PageSection id="work" title="What I do now">
    <p>
      {site.role} at {site.employer.name}: I sit with the client, find the step a person is doing by
      hand, and build whatever it takes to remove it. Sometimes that is product work, sometimes it
      is the systems underneath. <a href="/experience">The experience page</a> has the roles in
      detail, and <a href="/#projects">the projects</a> are the work I set myself.
    </p>
  </PageSection>

  <PageSection id="outside" title="Outside the work" ground="body">
    <Pending />
    {/* @TODO: anything you want here, or delete this section */}
  </PageSection>
</Base>
